From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0395-mac-lead-01-tensor-only-listed-programs.patch

Source: 0395-mac-lead-01-tensor-only-listed-programs.patch
Moved by hand: the list check sits after upstream's new title_tensor/EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=0 mode choice; upstream lowers Ocarina's networks by default now

shader: EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY lowers only the listed HMMA programs

EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY=<hex offset>,...: with EDEN_NX2_TENSOR set, a program is lowered only when its
first HMMA is at one of these byte offsets, the "instruction" of the rejection log. The offsets are
the same in run62, run66, run68 and run70, though the code addresses move. The rest stay rejected
with "matrix multiply" in the error, so they keep the stand-in. Unset, nothing changes.

Why: 10 of Ocarina's 11 rejected programs are the movie library's NDVE filter. They match nxnative
#1375/#1376: 10 programs, 13 dispatches, three of them twice. run68 reaches the stand-in for all of
them. run60 built exactly these 10 (10 "Compute pipeline built" lines) and never reached the 11th,
so its 15.7 s frame, 17 fps and stop came from NDVE alone. nxnative measures NDVE as 1.1/255 from a
plain copy on the movies. With this patch rebase-01 can be tried on the 11th alone:

  EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact
  EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY=ad0

Guess, not proven: that ad0 is what Kokiri's luma 0.29 against 0.10 depends on, and that gameplay
runs no NDVE program. Unknown: ad0's cost.

Checked off the console: a harness on this header with HMMA at the logged offsets. Unset, the
program is rejected as before; ONLY without TENSOR too; TENSOR=compact or 1 with ONLY=ad0 lowers a
program with HMMAs at ad0 and b00 and rejects b30 and 43c0 with "matrix multiply" in the error.
PS5-target clang syntax check. Applies on core16, and after rebase-01.

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
index 058a855da3..341df1baeb 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <bit>
 #include <span>
 #include <optional>
+#include <string>
 #include <string_view>
 #include <vector>
 #include "common/common_types.h"
@@ -208,6 +209,7 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
     bool main_exited = false;
     bool computed_branch = false; // a jump table: the program ends at its self-branch, not an EXIT
     bool uses_uniform_bank = false;
+    bool hmma_program_listed = false; // EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY passed this program's first HMMA
     const bool uses_async_copy = std::any_of(code.begin(), code.end(), [](const auto& instruction) {
         return instruction.Bits(0, 12) == 0xfae;
     });
@@ -1616,6 +1618,22 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
                                      : (tensor || title_tensor) ? "1"
                                                                 : nullptr;
             if (!mode) return fail(index, "native matrix multiply (set EDEN_NX2_TENSOR to emulate)");
+            // EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY=<hex offset>,...: lower only programs whose first HMMA is at one of
+            // these byte offsets (the "instruction" of the rejection log, the same in every run).
+            // The others stay rejected, so they keep the stand-in. Ocarina of Time: ad0 is the one
+            // program outside its movie library; the movie filter NDVE is 43c0, 1eb0, 790, 3440,
+            // 9f0, 2c40, ef0, 9a0, 1bb0 and b30, close to a plain copy on nxnative (#1375).
+            static const std::string tensor_only = [] {
+                const char* const text = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY");
+                return text ? "," + std::string{text} + "," : std::string{};
+            }();
+            if (!tensor_only.empty() && !hmma_program_listed) {
+                const std::string offset = fmt::format(",{:x},", index * sizeof(Instruction));
+                if (tensor_only.find(offset) == std::string::npos) {
+                    return fail(index, "native matrix multiply (not in EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_ONLY)");
+                }
+                hmma_program_listed = true;
+            }
             const u32 a = insn.Bits(24, 8), b = insn.Bits(32, 8), c = insn.Bits(64, 8);
             const u32 shape = insn.words[2] & ~0xffU;
             const u32 depth = shape == 0 ? 8U : 16U;
